The minister seals the intelligence, military and cabinet records against
destruction, publishes the team's appointment and recusal rules, and promises
neither an indictment nor an acquittal. Investigators must identify an act, an
available offence and admissible evidence before asking a court for anything.

Razem calls the refusal to promise prison evasive. Victims' lawyers answer that
a case built to survive disclosure and appeal is more than a photograph of an
old prime minister in handcuffs. The ministry gains a file whose conclusion it
does not control.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the evidence rules on the record

@public_account
title: Open a Sejm inquiry and reject imprisonment without a criminal case
subtitle: Establish political responsibility, publish the archive and pursue remedies without manufacturing an offence for holding office.
