A Sejm commission takes testimony in public, requests the state archive and
separates political responsibility from offences that prosecutors can already
investigate. Its report can recommend disclosure, institutional reform and
remedies; it cannot create a retroactive crime called a governmental record.

Razem loses the prison it asked for and gains hearings it can question under
oath. Miller receives no immunity: any specific criminal evidence remains with
ordinary prosecutors. Lewica accepts the harder distinction between exposing
what government did and ordering what a court must conclude.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the inquiry mandate
